In January 2025, Biggs announced his run for governor in the [[2026 Arizona gubernatorial election]].<ref>{{Cite news |work=[[KJZZ-TV]] |access-date=September 27, 2025 |author=Schutsky, Wayne |date=January 27, 2025 |url=https://www.kjzz.org/politics/2025-01-27/congressman-andy-biggs-officially-enters-2026-arizona-governors-race |title=Congressman Andy Biggs officially enters 2026 Arizona governor's race }}</ref> His opponents in the Republican primary included [[Karrin Taylor Robson]] (who later withdrew) and [[David Schweikert]].<ref>{{Cite news |work=[[Arizona Capitol Times]] |access-date=September 28, 2025 |author=Fischer, Howard |date=July 22, 2025 |url=https://www.kjzz.org/politics/2025-01-27/congressman-andy-biggs-officially-enters-2026-arizona-governors-race |title=Congressman Andy Biggs officially enters 2026 Arizona governor's race }}</ref>

